@prefix ds: <https://ds.canonical.com/>.
@prefix anatomy: <https://anatomy.canonical.com/>.
@prefix dt: <https://dt.canonical.com/>.

ds:apps_landscape.pattern.sortable_list a ds:Pattern;
    ds:name "Sortable List";
    ds:summary "Landscape's `SortableFieldList` pattern for reordering export columns through drag-and-drop, arrow buttons, or numeric position input. Each successful reorder calls `onOrderChange` with the full updated order. The component includes table display, reset to first-render order, optional group metadata chips, FLIP animation for moves, and focus restoration.\n\nMain use cases:\n\n- Let users reorder columns in the Landscape export workflow before final submission  \n- Provide multiple reorder paths: drag, arrow buttons, and direct numeric input for accessibility and touch support  \n- Show field groups or metadata alongside orderable columns  \n- Preserve and reset to the initial column order selected by the user";
    ds:anatomyDsl "node:\n  uri: ds:apps_landscape.pattern.sortable_list\n  role: export field reorder\n  edges:\n    - node:\n        role: instruction and reset block\n        edges:\n          - node:\n              role: instruction text\n              relation:\n                cardinality: \"1\"\n          - node:\n              uri: global.component.button\n              role: reset order\n              relation:\n                cardinality: \"1\"\n        relation:\n          cardinality: \"1\"\n    - node:\n        uri: global.component.modular-table\n        role: sortable field table\n        edges:\n          - node:\n              role: sortable item\n              edges:\n                - node:\n                    role: drag affordance\n                    description: Raw decorative Vanilla icon element using the p-icon--drag class; not a Canonical Icon component.\n                    relation:\n                      cardinality: \"1\"\n                - node:\n                    role: item label\n                    relation:\n                      cardinality: \"1\"\n                - node:\n                    uri: global.component.chip\n                    role: group metadata\n                    relation:\n                      cardinality: \"0..1\"\n                      condition: Rendered when groupTitle is truthy.\n                - node:\n                    role: order controls\n                    edges:\n                      - node:\n                          uri: global.component.button\n                          role: move down\n                          relation:\n                            cardinality: \"1\"\n                      - node:\n                          uri: global.component.input\n                          role: position input\n                          a11y:\n                            input.type: number\n                          relation:\n                            cardinality: \"1\"\n                      - node:\n                          uri: global.component.button\n                          role: move up\n                          relation:\n                            cardinality: \"1\"\n                    relation:\n                      cardinality: \"1\"\n              relation:\n                cardinality: \"0..*\"\n        relation:\n          cardinality: \"1\"\n    - node:\n        role: drag overlay\n        relation:\n          cardinality: \"0..1\"\n          condition: Rendered in a document-body portal while draggingFieldId is set.";
    ds:anatomyClassic "https://www.figma.com/design/I4WpvwMuQI6v1qhgUl63Sx/Landscape-Pragma-components?node-id=26-7&t=iG2ObZ6Q1XG2A2MB-4\n\nTable 65\n\n### Supporting hooks (implementation detail)\n\nTable 66\n\n";
    ds:usage "### When to use\n\n- Use in Landscape’s export review step to reorder selected `ExportField` records before submission.\n- Provide stable unique ids and unique, concise labels; ids drive row refs/state and labels drive accessible names.\n- Treat buttons and numeric input as the reliable non-drag paths, especially on touch devices.\n- Keep parent `fields` synchronized with `onOrderChange` when order is controlled externally.\n\n### When not to use\n\n**Display sorting or read-only sequences**\n\nWhen you need to show ordered items without user reordering capability.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Using this component in a read-only view where users only view a pre-sorted list.\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Use a basic table or list component without drag/reorder controls.\n\n**Hierarchical or cross-list movement**\n\nWhen items belong to different hierarchies or need to move between multiple lists.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Trying to drag items between different groups or parent containers within a single component instance.\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Build a hierarchical tree component or multi-list drag-and-drop system designed for cross-boundary reordering.\n\n**Arbitrary item shapes or reduced-motion requirement**\n\nWhen you need full reduced-motion support or the items don’t fit the export field model.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Using this component without disabling FLIP animations and drag-overlay motion for users with `prefers-reduced-motion`.\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Extract or build a headless sortable hook that respects motion preferences, or implement your own reorder logic for custom item shapes.";
    ds:guidelines "### Accessibility\n\n- Move buttons and position inputs include the field label in their accessible names. Same-direction focus restoration interpolates that label directly into a CSS attribute selector without escaping; labels containing selector-significant characters such as quotes or backslashes can make the selector unsafe, throw, or prevent focus restoration.\n- Endpoint buttons use Canonical disabled behavior; focus restoration intentionally skips a same-direction button that becomes `aria-disabled=\"true\"`.\n- The drag icon/row has no keyboard drag semantics, `aria-describedby`, or live instructions. The overlay is `aria-hidden`.\n- No live region announces changed positions, successful drops, or reset. Visible input values and focus movement are the only current nonvisual cues.\n- Table headers identify the two columns, but rows are draggable without a dedicated semantic handle.\n\n### Content\n\n- Instructions and reset copy are fixed English and export-specific; there are no content props.\n- Use human-readable labels and optional group titles; do not expose raw field ids.\n- “Reset order” means first-render order, not most recent server/prop order.\n\n### Internationalization / globalization\n\n- Instructions, table headers, reset label, and accessible-name templates are hardcoded English.\n- Numeric commit uses `Number.parseInt(raw, 10)` rather than locale parsing or input validity. Integer prefixes such as `2.5` parse as `2` if the browser permits the draft.\n- Positions and overlay badges use unformatted numbers; no RTL-specific drag/motion behavior exists.\n\n### Animation\n\n- Drag overlay position is updated imperatively through one coalesced animation frame per dragover burst.\n- Arrow/numeric moves use a `0.25s ease` FLIP transform, a `150ms` highlight, and smooth delayed `scrollIntoView`; drag rows use `0.15s` opacity/box-shadow transitions.\n- Source cancels tracked in-flight animation frames/timers before new FLIP capture and on unmount.\n- There is no `prefers-reduced-motion` media query or runtime branch. This is a current accessibility caveat.\n\n### Keyboard navigation and focus\n\n- DOM order is reset, then each row’s move-down button, number input, and move-up button.\n- Enter in the number input parses and commits an in-range different position. Invalid, empty, same, or out-of-range values clear the draft without callback; blur always clears the draft and does not commit.\n- Arrow-button moves request focus restoration to the moved row’s same-direction button. Numeric moves scroll/highlight but do not restore focus to the moved row.\n- A drag ending without successful drop restores the order captured at drag start. No custom Escape handler exists.\n\n### Device / layout\n\n- The order column is fixed at `10.5rem`; the number input is `5rem`. No component breakpoint or responsive table adaptation exists.\n- Overlay is portalled to `document.body`, fixed at the viewport origin and moved by transforms, with `z-index: 9999` and pointer events disabled.\n- Native HTML5 row dragging is unreliable on touch; buttons and numeric input are the current mobile path.\n- Long tables are not virtualized. Arrow/numeric movement smooth-scrolls the moved row to viewport center after motion.\n\n### Performance\n\n- Overlay movement avoids React state per dragover; row ref callbacks are cached by field id.\n- FLIP captures and updates every registered row, and each drag-enter reorders the full array. No upper bound or large-list benchmark is documented.\n- Ref callback cache entries are not pruned when fields disappear, although detached row elements are removed from the row map.";
    ds:tier ds:apps_landscape;
    ds:documentationStage ds:tag.specialadoption-docs;
    ds:hasProperty [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`fields`";
        ds:summary "Ordered field records with id, label, and optional group title. ";
        ds:propertyType "list of objects";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "TypeScript: `ExportField[]`, where `ExportField` is `{ id: string; label: string; groupTitle?: string }`. Ids must be stable and unique. First-render array contents become the permanent reset baseline for that mount. `SortableFieldListProps` is implementation-local, while the feature barrel separately exports `ExportField`. "
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`fields[].id`";
        ds:summary "Supplies the stable field identity used for row keys, refs, and reorder state. ";
        ds:propertyType "text";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "TypeScript: `string`. Must be unique within `fields`. "
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`fields[].label`";
        ds:summary "Supplies visible field text and text interpolated into accessible control names. ";
        ds:propertyType "text";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "TypeScript: `string`."
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`fields[].groupTitle`";
        ds:summary "Supplies optional group metadata rendered as a chip. ";
        ds:propertyType "text";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "TypeScript: `string`. Rendering requires a truthy value. ";
        ds:optional "true"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`onOrderChange`";
        ds:summary "Receives full order after successful drop, arrow/numeric move, or reset. ";
        ds:propertyType "callback";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "TypeScript: `(fields: ExportField[]) => void`, where `ExportField` is `{ id: string; label: string; groupTitle?: string }`. Called synchronously; source does not await, catch, or roll back callback failures. `SortableFieldListProps` is implementation-local; the feature barrel does not export a generic `SortableList` symbol or props type. "
    ].
